Bell Field - Service Done Right.

Field Dispatch Service Software.

Windows 10/11 x Android
-----------------------------------------------------------------


The shape of the product

This should be three surfaces, not one giant app:

1. Office app

This is the “desktop software,” but it should really be a desktop-focused web app, not a Windows-native program.
That gives you:

fast development
easier updates
easier remote access
easier role-based access
no install headaches

This is where dispatch, CSR, managers, accounting, and office staff live.

2. Field app

This should be a real mobile app, not just a stretched website.

Reason: techs need:

offline tolerance
camera/photos
signatures
fast load times
easy tap targets
local caching
reliable job access in bad signal areas
3. Shared backend

One backend should own all business rules and be the single source of truth.

The field app and office app should never talk directly to each other.
They both talk to the backend.

How I would split the code

Use a modular monolith.

That means:

one main backend
one main database
clearly separated modules inside it
strict module boundaries
internal events for cross-module updates

Do not start with microservices.

Repo layout
/apps
  /office-web
  /field-mobile
  /api
  /worker

/packages
  /ui-office
  /ui-mobile
